# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Evidence / log vocabulary

Established: {{DATE}}

This file catalogs the known output and log families for {{PROJECT_NAME}}. It grows
incrementally: add a new entry the first time you encounter a new source type during
a diagnostic pass. The diagnostic role reads this file as its starting map; the
orchestrator updates it as the project matures.

---

## Per-entry format

```
### <Family name>
Location: <path pattern, e.g. `{{ROOT}}/logs/**/*.log` or `{{ROOT}}/outputs/*.csv`>
Format: <plain text | JSON | CSV | binary | other>
Produced by: <what generates this — a script, a service, a job, a test run>
Cadence: <when it appears — per-run, per-day, on-error, manually>
Key signals: <what to look for — error prefixes, field names, anomaly patterns>
Notes: <anything else a diagnostic agent needs to know>
```

---

## Lines that are normal

A line you have seen and know to be normal output can be recorded as a bullet that starts with
`normal:` (`expected:` works too). A trailing `*` matches every line that begins with that text. A
leading timestamp is ignored. The two bullets below are examples: replace them with your own.

- normal: `example service started *`
- normal: `example heartbeat ok seq=1`

The bullets are a record of what quiet output looks like, so a reader can set those lines aside.

